<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ request.locale.iso_code }}">
  <head>
    {% # Charset and viewport first, then title, SEO and social tags %}
    {% render 'meta-tags' %}

    {% comment %}
      Fonts. Both faces are declared in snippets/css-variables.liquid with
      asset_url, so these preloads resolve to the same versioned URLs and the
      browser makes one request per font. Satoshi carries every heading
      weight; Nunito Sans is the body face, cut down to Latin and its weight
      axis (38 KB). Both preload so the bold headings and body copy above the
      fold do not swap in late and shift the buy box; font-display: swap in
      the @font-face keeps text visible while they load.
    {% endcomment %}
    {{ 'satoshi-variable.woff2' | asset_url | preload_tag: as: 'font', type: 'font/woff2', crossorigin: 'anonymous' }}
    {{ 'nunito-sans-variable.woff2' | asset_url | preload_tag: as: 'font', type: 'font/woff2', crossorigin: 'anonymous' }}

    {% # Inlined CSS variables and @font-face %}
    {% render 'css-variables' %}

    {% comment %}
      The compiled Tailwind stylesheet, inlined so first paint does not wait
      on a stylesheet request. Shopify's inline_asset_content filter stops at
      15 KB, so the build writes the CSS into snippets/critical-css.liquid
      instead (scripts/build-critical-snippet.js, run by npm run build:css).
    {% endcomment %}
    <style>{% render 'critical-css' %}</style>

    {% comment %}
      Lenis smooth-scroll. Loaded on every page; smooth-scroll.js gates
      itself to desktop (≥1024px, fine pointer) and bails under
      prefers-reduced-motion. defer keeps lenis.min.js → smooth-scroll.js
      execution order.
    {% endcomment %}
    <script src="{{ 'lenis.min.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
    <script src="{{ 'smooth-scroll.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

    {% comment %}
      The one dialog behaviour, shared by the newsletter and scratch offer
      popups (snippets/modal-dialog.liquid). Deferred, so it runs after parsing
      but before DOMContentLoaded — which is what the section scripts wait on.
    {% endcomment %}
    <script src="{{ 'aira-modal.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

    {% comment %}
      Lazy video: promotes the data-src sources that snippets/lazy-video.liquid
      ships and plays each video only once it is near the viewport. Deferred,
      like the modal script, so section scripts can rely on window.airaLazyVideo.
    {% endcomment %}
    <script src="{{ 'lazy-video.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

    {% # Favicon — theme setting if set, otherwise the aira logo mark %}
    {%- if settings.favicon != blank -%}
      <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 32, height: 32 }}">
      <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 180, height: 180 }}">
    {%- else -%}
      {% comment %}
        The mark on its own navy tile, so it stays visible on a light tab bar
        and on a dark one. Earlier versions were a bare mark with no ground:
        the white one vanished into light tabs, the navy one into dark tabs.

        SVG first for anything that takes it, since it stays crisp at any size.
        The PNGs are not belt and braces: apple-touch-icon ignores SVG outright,
        so without favicon-180 an iOS home screen bookmark falls back to a
        screenshot of the page. 512 is there for the Android install prompt.
        All three are rendered from favicon.svg, so re-export together.
      {% endcomment %}
      <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="{{ 'favicon.svg' | asset_url }}">
      <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="512x512" href="{{ 'favicon-512.png' | asset_url }}">
      <link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="180x180" href="{{ 'favicon-180.png' | asset_url }}">
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      Judge.me scroll-hijack guard.
      The Judge.me reviews widget calls window.scrollTo({behavior:'smooth'})
      twice on mount/rerender (once at ~4s, again at ~7s post-load), jerking
      the page to its own anchor — even when the user is already scrolled
      there. Since the `behavior` option is passed per-call, no amount of CSS
      can stop it. This monkey-patch must run BEFORE Judge.me's bundle loads
      (which arrives via content_for_header), so it sits here.

      It only swallows calls whose stack trace points back into Judge.me's
      bundle — own anchor links, scrollIntoView on user interactions, and
      every other consumer of these APIs pass through unaffected.

      Remove if Judge.me ships a setting to disable this, or if Judge.me is
      uninstalled.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <script>
      (function () {
        function fromJudgeme() {
          try {
            var s = new Error().stack || '';
            return s.indexOf('judgeme') !== -1 || s.indexOf('ReviewWidget') !== -1;
          } catch (e) { return false; }
        }

        var winScrollTo = window.scrollTo;
        window.scrollTo = function () {
          if (fromJudgeme()) return;
          return winScrollTo.apply(window, arguments);
        };

        var winScroll = window.scroll;
        window.scroll = function () {
          if (fromJudgeme()) return;
          return winScroll.apply(window, arguments);
        };

        if (Element.prototype.scrollTo) {
          var elScrollTo = Element.prototype.scrollTo;
          Element.prototype.scrollTo = function () {
            if (fromJudgeme()) return;
            return elScrollTo.apply(this, arguments);
          };
        }

        if (Element.prototype.scrollIntoView) {
          var elScrollIntoView = Element.prototype.scrollIntoView;
          Element.prototype.scrollIntoView = function () {
            if (fromJudgeme()) return;
            return elScrollIntoView.apply(this, arguments);
          };
        }
      })();
    </script>

    {{ content_for_header }}
  </head>

  <body>
    {% sections 'header-group' %}

    {{ content_for_layout }}

    {% sections 'footer-group' %}

    {% render 'cart-drawer' %}

    {% comment %}
      Site-wide launch offer popup. A static section rather than a snippet so
      its copy and timing stay editable in the theme editor. The QR insert's
      10% off popup is a separate section, on the homepage template only.
    {% endcomment %}
    {% section 'scratch-offer-popup' %}
  </body>
</html>
